Sound Evidence: A Unified Evidence Framework for Audio Forensics
Authors listed on the submission: Ze Yu, Haiwei Wu, Gao Chang, Yuanman Li,
Jiantao Zhou. Research source and supplied checkpoints belong to their
respective rights holders. This candidate does not choose or grant an open
source license. The authors must select the source-code and checkpoint
licenses before public release. No third-party dataset recordings are bundled.

The registered CPSFactorial-v2 implementation is preserved byte-for-byte in
src/sound_evidence/_core.py. New runtime/CLI wrappers provide packaging,
checkpoint-schema loading and portable paths; they do not change that file.
SOURCE_BINDINGS.json records source-relative identifiers and content hashes.
The three bundled far_full checkpoints are from the original formal core
matrix, not later same-semantics or rebuttal reruns. Generated demo audio is
mathematical test material with no claimed forensic ground truth.
